      en: "Moanda is a town in Haut-Ogooué Province, known for its manganese mining. The mine opened in 1957 by Compagnie Minière de l'Ogooué (COMILOG). Moanda holds one of the world's largest manganese deposits, estimated at 250 million tonnes of ore. Mining is open-pit. Ore is transported by cable car to the border, then by rail to Owendo port. The mine is the region's main economic driver. Moanda has about 60,000 inhabitants, growing through miner migration. Annual production is around 4 million tonnes.",
