      en: "Baraka Mission Station was founded in 1842 by American Protestant missionaries near Libreville. It was the first Christian mission in Gabon. The station included a church, a school, and a printing press. Missionaries translated the Bible into Mpongwe. After many missionaries died from tropical diseases, the station was handed over to French Catholics in 1870. Today only foundations remain. The site is a national sanctuary. Annual memorial services are held.",
